# C++ Basics

## getline
Used to read an entire line (including spaces) from input.

```cpp
string str;
getline(cin, str);
cout << str;
```
> Whole line entered becomes the output â€” unlike `cin >>` which stops at space.

## Vectors

```cpp
vector<int> v;
v.push_back(5);     // add to end
v.emplace_back(6);  // faster than push_back for objects

// Iterate using iterator
for (vector<int>::iterator it = v.begin(); it != v.end(); it++) {
    cout << *it << " ";
}

// Simpler with auto
for (auto x : v) cout << x << " ";
```

